IELTS.lesson({"test": 4, "part": 3, "title": "Test 4, Part 3 — the discussion", "candidate": "rawan", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "We've been talking about an app or a website you use a lot, and I'd like to discuss with you one or two more general questions related to this.", "ar": "كنّا نتحدّث عن تطبيق أو موقع تستخدمينه كثيراً، وأودّ أن أناقش معكِ سؤالاً أو سؤالين أعمّ يتعلّقان بهذا.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/63b1ea0f97b55599.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's consider technology and work.", "ar": "لنتناول التكنولوجيا والعمل.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/64b58781f8dbb8fe.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How has technology changed the kind of work people do?", "ar": "كيف غيّرت التكنولوجيا نوع العمل الذي يقوم به الناس؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/71559d59692f7100.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "It's changed who you're competing with more than what you do, I'd say. The design I do isn't different from design twenty years ago. But twenty years ago I'd have been competing with people in Damascus, and now it's everybody with a laptop. That cuts both ways, obviously. It's also why I have clients at all.", "ar": "أقول إنّها غيّرت من تنافسينه أكثر مما غيّرت ما تفعلينه. التصميم الذي أقوم به لا يختلف عن التصميم قبل عشرين سنة. لكن قبل عشرين سنة كنت سأنافس أناساً في دمشق، أمّا الآن فأنافس كلّ من لديه حاسوب محمول. ولهذا وجهان طبعاً. فهو أيضاً سبب وجود زبائن لي أصلاً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/e1f8007882121aad.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Some people say technology has made work more stressful. Would you agree?", "ar": "يقول بعض الناس إنّ التكنولوجيا جعلت العمل أكثر إرهاقاً. هل توافقينهم؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/568f8f2c0290650b.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Yes, though usually for the wrong reason. It isn't the volume. It's that the boundary went, so there's no moment where work is over and it's never over. Having said that, I chose this, and most people I know in Damascus didn't get to choose anything about their work at all.", "ar": "نعم، لكن عادةً للسبب الخطأ. ليست المسألة في الكمّية. المسألة أنّ الحدّ الفاصل اختفى، فلم تعد هناك لحظة ينتهي عندها العمل، وبالتالي لا ينتهي أبداً. ومع ذلك، أنا اخترت هذا، ومعظم من أعرفهم في دمشق لم يختاروا شيئاً في عملهم إطلاقاً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/133fef83111c39cd.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Will more people work from home in the future?", "ar": "هل سيعمل عدد أكبر من الناس من البيت في المستقبل؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/32a62688855ae187.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "More, yes, but I think it'll separate into two different things that we're currently calling the same thing. There's working from home because your company allows it, and there's working from home because you have no company. Almost nobody I know in Damascus is in the first group, and my guess is we end up with different words for them.", "ar": "أكثر، نعم، لكنّي أظنّ أنّه سينقسم إلى أمرين مختلفين نسمّيهما اليوم بالاسم نفسه. هناك العمل من البيت لأنّ شركتك تسمح بذلك، وهناك العمل من البيت لأنّه لا شركة لك. لا أحد تقريباً ممن أعرفهم في دمشق في المجموعة الأولى، وتخميني أنّنا سننتهي إلى كلمتين مختلفتين لهما.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/726f79fd56a50ab7.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now let's talk about information and trust.", "ar": "والآن لنتحدّث عن المعلومات والثقة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/84f47678918964d2.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it harder to know what information to trust now?", "ar": "هل صار من الأصعب معرفة أيّ معلومة نثق بها الآن؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4d9b653440f7426a.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Harder, or just more obvious that it always was? I'd say the second, mostly. My father trusted one newspaper and one television channel completely, and that wasn't better information. There was simply less visible disagreement. What's genuinely new is how much of it there is.", "ar": "أصعب، أم صار أوضح فقط أنّه كان كذلك دائماً؟ أقول الثاني في معظمه. أبي كان يثق بصحيفة واحدة وقناة تلفزيونيّة واحدة ثقة كاملة، ولم تكن تلك معلومات أفضل. كان الخلاف الظاهر أقلّ ببساطة. الجديد فعلاً هو كمّ المعلومات.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/6e77c4f2fafd9864.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How do people decide what to believe online?", "ar": "كيف يقرّر الناس بماذا يصدّقون على الإنترنت؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/54d0c15a583be057.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Whoever says it first and confidently, which is a terrible system. Take anything about the electricity. There'll be an official number, and there'll be what everyone in the building actually experiences, and people believe the building. Which is often right, and still isn't reasoning.", "ar": "من يقوله أوّلاً وبثقة، وهذا نظام سيّئ جداً. خذ أيّ شيء عن الكهرباء. سيكون هناك رقم رسمي، وسيكون هناك ما يعيشه فعلاً كلّ من في المبنى، والناس يصدّقون المبنى. وهذا صحيح في أغلب الأحيان، ومع ذلك ليس تفكيراً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/7cf997c6ab568f7a.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Should companies be responsible for the information on their platforms?", "ar": "هل ينبغي أن تكون الشركات مسؤولة عن المعلومات على منصّاتها؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5bc0da6ef4661b71.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Partly, and I say that reluctantly, because I don't love the idea of a company deciding what's true. But the alternative is pretending they're only a pipe, and they aren't. They choose what gets seen, and so does everybody forwarding it on the street. If you choose, you're responsible. You can't have the first without the second.", "ar": "جزئياً، وأقول ذلك على مضض، لأنّني لا أحبّ فكرة أن تقرّر شركة ما هو الصحيح. لكنّ البديل هو التظاهر بأنّها مجرّد أنبوب، وهي ليست كذلك. هي تختار ما يُرى، وكذلك يفعل كلّ من يعيد إرساله في الشارع. ومن يختار يتحمّل المسؤوليّة. لا يمكنك أن تأخذ الأوّل دون الثاني.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/8dec11c5fc628366.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of the speaking test.", "ar": "شكراً لكِ. بهذا ينتهي اختبار المحادثة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f502144bdfbbc476.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "How has technology changed the kind of work people do?", "topic": "Technology and work", "model": "It's changed who you're competing with more than what you do, I'd say. The design I do isn't different from design twenty years ago. But twenty years ago I'd have been competing with people in Damascus, and now it's everybody with a laptop. That cuts both ways, obviously. It's also why I have clients at all.", "modelBand": 7.5, "why": "CONTRAST"}, {"q": "Some people say technology has made work more stressful. Would you agree?", "topic": "Technology and work", "model": "Yes, though usually for the wrong reason. It isn't the volume. It's that the boundary went, so there's no moment where work is over and it's never over. Having said that, I chose this, and most people I know in Damascus didn't get to choose anything about their work at all.", "modelBand": 7.5, "why": "CONCEDE"}, {"q": "Will more people work from home in the future?", "topic": "Technology and work", "model": "More, yes, but I think it'll separate into two different things that we're currently calling the same thing. There's working from home because your company allows it, and there's working from home because you have no company. Almost nobody I know in Damascus is in the first group, and my guess is we end up with different words for them.", "modelBand": 7.5, "why": "SPECULATE"}, {"q": "Is it harder to know what information to trust now?", "topic": "Information and trust", "model": "Harder, or just more obvious that it always was? I'd say the second, mostly. My father trusted one newspaper and one television channel completely, and that wasn't better information. There was simply less visible disagreement. What's genuinely new is how much of it there is.", "modelBand": 7.5, "why": "QUALIFY"}, {"q": "How do people decide what to believe online?", "topic": "Information and trust", "model": "Whoever says it first and confidently, which is a terrible system. Take anything about the electricity. There'll be an official number, and there'll be what everyone in the building actually experiences, and people believe the building. Which is often right, and still isn't reasoning.", "modelBand": 7.5, "why": "EXEMPLIFY"}, {"q": "Should companies be responsible for the information on their platforms?", "topic": "Information and trust", "model": "Partly, and I say that reluctantly, because I don't love the idea of a company deciding what's true. But the alternative is pretending they're only a pipe, and they aren't. They choose what gets seen, and so does everybody forwarding it on the street. If you choose, you're responsible. You can't have the first without the second.", "modelBand": 7.5, "why": "CONCEDE"}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120"}});
